with synthetic plastic production, plastic pollution, greenhouse gas emissions associated with landfill waste and food waste management may be mitigated simultaneously. Such industrial symbioses align with at least 10 of the 17 United Nations Sustainable Development Goals. Chitosan is a biodegradable, non-toxic polymer with potential use in a range of disposable plastic applications. We describe characteristics of chitosan, the global chitosan market, how chitosan can be modified into different types of bio-based plastics, and we highlight challenges and constraints.","author_count":5,"author_ids":["A5030937684","A5060683753","A5069707113","A5089559628","A5091211384"],"author_institution_ids":["I4210097978","I4210146959","I4210151987","I84218800"],"authors":[{"id":"A5030937684","name":"Christian Nansen"},{"id":"A5091211384","name":"Ryan Meadows"},{"id":"A5060683753","name":"Trevor M. Fowles"},{"id":"A5089559628","name":"Patrice Jacob Savi"},{"id":"A5069707113","name":"Pamela Estefan\u00eda Andrade"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":0,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.3390/su182010302","domain_tags":[],"facet_tags":["matrix:food_and_drink"],"institution_ids":["I4210097978","I4210146959","I4210151987","I84218800"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Sustainability","last_updated":"2026-10-12T09:40:04.860316","license":"cc-by","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"gold","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/su182010302","openalex_topics":["T10488","T10753","T12336"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T12336","pub_date":"2026-10-10","study_type":"article","title":"Mass-Rearing of Insects on Food Waste to Produce Chitosan\u2014A Bio-Based Plastic Alternative","type":"article","work_id":"W7221336842","year":2026}]}
